{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1192927-nova-sterility-thoughts","id":1192927,"title":"Nova Sterility Thoughts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aberrant"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-07T19:40:46-08:00","id":1192927,"title":"Nova Sterility Thoughts","content":"Was just wondering what others thought of the sterility cocktail aspect of the 1e Aberrant setting. Whether you kept it, discarded it, changed it or something else. Additionally was are your thoughts on it being present in 2e. <br /> <br /> Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T21:28:47-08:00","id":1192957,"title":"","content":"One idea that crossed my mind (that I'm not married too) is that the nature of the N-Day event has resulted in many (though not all) Novas being sterile without it being part of an intentional conspiracy. A Nova having a kid is a big deal in this scenario, but not unheard of. Meanwhile some conspiracy theorists claim Utopia is behind sterilizations, but they're wrong.<br /> <br /> I'm really torn, because I do think there needs to be stuff for &quot;Aberrant&quot; to legitimately rebel against - and if anything I'd like to see them expand this edition from being the reaction against a specific conspiracy, to more of a political movement that (unlike Terragen) embraces the Zurich Accords and the human-equality-status of Novas and (unlike Project Utopia) believes they should be unchecked equal citizens who don't owe the public anything beyond other citizens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T23:26:48-08:00","id":1192986,"title":"","content":"A thought to consider:<br /> <br /> You guys know my love of Anne McCaffrey. In her &quot;Crystal Singer&quot; series, the titular singers are physiologically modified by a microbial symbiont. Among the abilities they gain are sharper senses and fairly rapid tissue regeneration. A severe injury that might have a normal human in recovery for months might take as many as a couple of weeks to heal for a crystal singer.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, while the symbiont tunes a singer's physiology for individual survival, it's at the cost of survival of the species: all crystal singers are sterile.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T23:49:00-08:00","id":1192989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1192927-nova-sterility-thoughts?p=1192986#post1192986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">all crystal singers are sterile.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm having a hard time putting into words just how much I dislike introducing this idea into Aberrant as a fact, and not a &quot;tin foil hat&quot; theory. 2nd generation Novas, and all the stories that they entail; trying to balance family and your duty/feelings of personal responsibility, generational stories, descending from powerful lineages, emerging from the shadow of greatness, etc... just... no... I think I dislike this more then Max Mercer... and that's quite a lot...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T00:01:25-08:00","id":1192992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1192927-nova-sterility-thoughts?p=1192989#post1192989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm having a hard time putting into words just how much I dislike introducing this idea into Aberrant as a fact, and not a &quot;tin foil hat&quot; theory. 2nd generation Novas, and all the stories that they entail; trying to balance family and your duty/feelings of personal responsibility, generational stories, descending from powerful lineages, emerging from the shadow of greatness, etc... just... no... I think I dislike this more then Max Mercer... and that's quite a lot...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think that particular 2nd Gen Nova narrative particularly works though if they're a rarity, which does require widespread sterility.<br /> <br /> Because otherwise you have the unavoidable eventual subsumation of the species issue. Not to mention hereditary power as a biological reality rather than political contrivance in the mean time.<br /> <br /> So I agree with you that infertility shouldn't be universal, but it should definitely be widespread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T00:10:56-08:00","id":1192995,"title":"","content":"What I think of is the Earth X Trilogy, where the Terrigen Mists are spread over the Earth and its as if the whole world has become a society of Mutants, though actually they are now realized Inhumans. The thing was fertility hit rock bottom after this, and with the return of the Inhuman Royal family there was an explanation that Inhumans have a very low fertility rate but the Inhuman civilization could get around this through very specific controlled breeding, hence why the royal family usually had arranged marriages. The thing was in this setting the Inhumans also were virtually unaging, and humans with superpowers activated by things other then Terrigenesis could still breed like Ben Grimm (cosmic rays) and Alicia Masters (Terragenesis), or Him and Her (Adam Warlock and his mate two artificial perfect humans).<br /> <br /> So how many of the Aberrants are over a hundred years old in the Aeon setting? Are the space Aberrants breed from human turned Aberrants or Aberrant breeding? Is Aberrant Breeding with normal Humans easier in anyway then breeding with other Aberrants? Do all Aberrants have increased lifespan?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T00:21:58-08:00","id":1192998,"title":"","content":"I have no issue with 1e's presentation of a &quot;sterility drug&quot; answer to that question. It gives players something to discover, and work on curing that will have global impact. It's great story fodder. My concern is that 2e seems to be... how do I put this... forgetting, or refusing, to bait the story hooks... Here's an example from Aeon: &quot;In the section\u2019s history, only one agent has ever gone rogue, and he was quickly apprehended by his fellow Minerva members.&quot; One rogue agent. Who are they? What are they doing now? Why did they go rogue? ... So many questions, but instead they've already been captured... good job writer... you killed it... the plot hook is dead... and I'm afraid that given the same pool of writers, that they will make the same mistake, and just write off the whole Nova Sterility plot as &quot;Novas just can't get pregnant, end of story.&quot; and &quot;end of story&quot; would be right...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T00:39:05-08:00","id":1193005,"title":"","content":"But aren't they still free to say that's the official story, and the Rogue Agent was never actually captured or faked his capture? I feel maybe they want to mention a lot of plot points and maybe elaborate later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T00:46:41-08:00","id":1193007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1192927-nova-sterility-thoughts?p=1193005#post1193005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But aren't they still free to say that's the official story, and the Rogue Agent was never actually captured or faked his capture? I feel maybe they want to mention a lot of plot points and maybe elaborate later.</div> </div> </div> </div>We are still free to do so in our own games, I know I will, but I highly doubt that anything is going to officially change as far as lost plot hooks goes. I'm all for mentioning plot points and never really elaborating on them again, but that's not what they did. They created a plot hook (The rogue agent) and then killed it (he was quickly apprehended) all in the same waste of the word count sentence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T00:56:11-08:00","id":1193009,"title":"","content":"I also have no problem with the sterility conspiracy being a conspiracy for players to solve. But you need to make it bigger, not smaller, so that it takes nova-level characters to unpick it and destroy it. (Or subvert it to their own ends, if that\u2019s what the players want.) <br /> <br /> It needs to be bigger than Utopia giving people who walk through their door an injection, and that\u2019s it. That\u2019s simple and easy to solve. It needs to be spread wider through the ecosystem - in the water, in the food, in cosmetics, in clothing. The conspiracy behind it has seeded it everywhere, so much everywhere, that it\u2019s difficult to tell if it is a conspiracy or whether it\u2019s the natural world being intrinsically against novas.<br /> <br /> It doesn\u2019t need to be hard to discover. One of the 1e problems was that it was laughably easy to detect for any nova with a certain set of skills or powers, and only moderately difficult to discover for novas without those abilities. Make it easy to discover - that\u2019s not the challenge. As per above, the challenge is discovering whether anyone is actually behind it (they are), and convincing others that it\u2019s not just natural.<br /> <br /> Make it difficult to cure. Various novas should have been able to easily shake off the sterilization, but make it more of a challenging quest in 2e. The way to do this is relatively simple - make the affliction psi based*. The conspiracy doesn\u2019t know why this special compound is so anti nova (and harmless to normal humans), but they know that it is. This gives story hooks and a trail of evidence that goes way back, to some group who studied stalwarts and Mesmerists, and noticed a tiny but statistically significant adversarial aspect to how their powers worked. Maybe this original group had no negative implications - maybe they just studied. But somewhere along the way, when novas appeared, someone else got hold of their research and synthesised the chemical and worked out how to make it global.<br /> <br /> (Maybe some lost, solitary Doyen was stranded on Earth, couldn\u2019t escape out of the barrier, and used its psi powers to modify Eath chemistry and organisms to produce this chemical as a terrified form of self Defence.)<br /> <br /> A conspiracy is fine, IMO, but it needs to be something to be defeated. In the 1e games I ran, this was certainly the case, but it was too easy to discover and defeat.<br /> <br /> * But such tiny amounts of psi that it does nothing to hinder the novas powers, but is incredibly hard for anything quantum-based to remove.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","user":"Bunyip","date":". 03-08-2018, 03:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T01:06:59-08:00","id":1193012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1192927-nova-sterility-thoughts?p=1193009#post1193009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Awesome</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes!<br /> <br /> This!<br /> <br /> 1,000x this!<br /> <br /> This is what I'm talking about. Make it something that's worthy of an entire campaign, not &quot;The M_R Node makes Novas sterile&quot;. That's boring, and we already have too many answers, and not enough questions in the TC. Novas <i>need</i> questions. I'm praying, and begging, that whoever writes TC: Aberrant does so with the intent of leaving 2 questions for every answer they reveal. TC and TC: Aeon did not do this, and I feel that their games are poorer for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T01:14:17-08:00","id":1193015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1192927-nova-sterility-thoughts?p=1192989#post1192989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm having a hard time putting into words just how much I dislike introducing this idea into Aberrant as a fact, and not a &quot;tin foil hat&quot; theory. 2nd generation Novas, and all the stories that they entail; trying to balance family and your duty/feelings of personal responsibility, generational stories, descending from powerful lineages, emerging from the shadow of greatness, etc... just... no... I think I dislike this more then Max Mercer... and that's quite a lot...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I think that if Novas were inherently sterile, I'd probably nope out of the line. That's enough to take it from my favourite game in the line, to not bothering at all. <br /> <br /> For me, Novas work because they're a possible future for humanity - There are problems, and it all goes wrong, but if it hadn't, humanity genuinely had the chance to become gods. That's <i>why</i> it's a tragedy. <br /> <br /> On a personal level, it completely kills a couple of my favourite Nova characters (and concepts). I've played several characters who were largely on board with separation between humans and novas. Basically, the non-batshit crazy Teragen. People who like humanity, think it's fine, but accept that they're not really a part of it, so want to go off and do their own thing, be their own people. <br /> <br /> Also, given that being a Nova makes it more likely for other people around you to erupt, it suddenly gets a bit gross. I don't want to play a character who's causing sterility in other people (... Not unless I actively take the &quot;Emits radiation&quot; aberration, anyway).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2649-tarion","name":"Tarion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T01:28:14-08:00","id":1193016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tarion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1192927-nova-sterility-thoughts?p=1193015#post1193015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I think that if Novas were inherently sterile, I'd probably nope out of the line. That's enough to take it from my favourite game in the line, to not bothering at all.<br /> <br /> For me, Novas work because they're a possible future for humanity - There are problems, and it all goes wrong, but if it hadn't, humanity genuinely had the chance to become gods. That's <i>why</i> it's a tragedy.<br /> <br /> On a personal level, it completely kills a couple of my favourite Nova characters (and concepts). I've played several characters who were largely on board with separation between humans and novas. Basically, the non-batshit crazy Teragen. People who like humanity, think it's fine, but accept that they're not really a part of it, so want to go off and do their own thing, be their own people.<br /> <br /> Also, given that being a Nova makes it more likely for other people around you to erupt, it suddenly gets a bit gross. I don't want to play a character who's causing sterility in other people (... Not unless I actively take the &quot;Emits radiation&quot; aberration, anyway).</div> </div> </div> </div>Quite a few of the people I know and game with bought into this KS... if Novas are all sterile, I know for a fact that none of us would back the KS for TC: Aberrant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T02:26:54-08:00","id":1193023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1192927-nova-sterility-thoughts?p=1193016#post1193016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Quite a few of the people I know and game with bought into this KS... if Novas are all sterile, I know for a fact that none of us would back the KS for TC: Aberrant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Based on your reaction to my earlier post, I assume you mean \u2018if novas are all irreversibly sterile without reasons that can be explored dramatically\u2019. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T02:27:18-08:00","id":1193024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1192927-nova-sterility-thoughts?p=1193012#post1193012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes!<br /> <br /> This!<br /> <br /> 1,000x this!<br /> <br /> This is what I'm talking about. Make it something that's worthy of an entire campaign, not &quot;The M_R Node makes Novas sterile&quot;. That's boring, and we already have too many answers, and not enough questions in the TC. Novas <i>need</i> questions. I'm praying, and begging, that whoever writes TC: Aberrant does so with the intent of leaving 2 questions for every answer they reveal. TC and TC: Aeon did not do this, and I feel that their games are poorer for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel the option to make it unimportant needs to be there. YES having the potential to make it a campaign concept is nice, but it being a mandatory conspiracy almost makes ignoring it and focusing on other issues seem missing the point. I feel both the option that its a super big story hook and its something you can casually ignore should be there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T03:09:58-08:00","id":1193030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1192927-nova-sterility-thoughts?p=1193024#post1193024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel the option to make it unimportant needs to be there. YES having the potential to make it a campaign concept is nice, but it being a mandatory conspiracy almost makes ignoring it and focusing on other issues seem missing the point. I feel both the option that its a super big story hook and its something you can casually ignore should be there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Changes like this are something I like in Aeon - Because 1st ed Trinity had so many big problems that if the players weren't running around putting out fires, the world ended. <br /> <br /> It's nice to be able to run campaigns that don't focus on the big conflict without having to take a machete to the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2649-tarion","name":"Tarion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T03:56:53-08:00","id":1193041,"title":"","content":"Wow all. This is great. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'm also going to say, all Novas are sterile as matter of course as being not enjoyable. At all. <br /> <br /> I like the idea of the potential of say an all nova species or society. A potential gone if everyone is sterile. <br /> <br /> As well it removes the Incredibles like story of a family and it's dynamics. <br /> <br /> That said: <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1192927-nova-sterility-thoughts?p=1193009#post1193009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also have no problem with the sterility conspiracy being a conspiracy for players to solve. But you need to make it bigger, not smaller, so that it takes nova-level characters to unpick it and destroy it. (Or subvert it to their own ends, if that\u2019s what the players want.) <br /> <br /> It needs to be bigger than Utopia giving people who walk through their door an injection, and that\u2019s it. That\u2019s simple and easy to solve. It needs to be spread wider through the ecosystem - in the water, in the food, in cosmetics, in clothing. The conspiracy behind it has seeded it everywhere, so much everywhere, that it\u2019s difficult to tell if it is a conspiracy or whether it\u2019s the natural world being intrinsically against novas.<br /> <br /> It doesn\u2019t need to be hard to discover. One of the 1e problems was that it was laughably easy to detect for any nova with a certain set of skills or powers, and only moderately difficult to discover for novas without those abilities. Make it easy to discover - that\u2019s not the challenge. As per above, the challenge is discovering whether anyone is actually behind it (they are), and convincing others that it\u2019s not just natural.<br /> <br /> Make it difficult to cure. Various novas should have been able to easily shake off the sterilization, but make it more of a challenging quest in 2e. The way to do this is relatively simple - make the affliction psi based*. The conspiracy doesn\u2019t know why this special compound is so anti nova (and harmless to normal humans), but they know that it is. This gives story hooks and a trail of evidence that goes way back, to some group who studied stalwarts and Mesmerists, and noticed a tiny but statistically significant adversarial aspect to how their powers worked. Maybe this original group had no negative implications - maybe they just studied. But somewhere along the way, when novas appeared, someone else got hold of their research and synthesised the chemical and worked out how to make it global.<br /> <br /> (Maybe some lost, solitary Doyen was stranded on Earth, couldn\u2019t escape out of the barrier, and used its psi powers to modify Eath chemistry and organisms to produce this chemical as a terrified form of self Defence.)<br /> <br /> A conspiracy is fine, IMO, but it needs to be something to be defeated. In the 1e games I ran, this was certainly the case, but it was too easy to discover and defeat.<br /> <br /> * But such tiny amounts of psi that it does nothing to hinder the novas powers, but is incredibly hard for anything quantum-based to remove.</div> </div> </div> </div>This! Very much this. <br /> <br /> Having it be the Doyen begins the scenes is a perfect the in. A perfect &quot;hey all so the settings are linked&quot; nod. Not too in your face just something cool. <br /> <br /> May be part of the problem is that the Galtea explosion had some effects on the environment and the Doyen used that, invisibly of course, to hide the manipulations. <br /> <br /> So like publically a lot of 1st gen Novas are sterile, but not all. The secrets chapter could say &quot;this can be am accident, or a conspiracy. If it's an accident then is mostly die to x, such as the radiation put out by the explosion. If it's a conspiracy here are two possibilities - human or alien - both involve psi. <br /> <br /> But yeah having all quantum using people naturally sterile seems to limit stories and campaigns more then it helps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T05:47:43-08:00","id":1193070,"title":"","content":"My personal preference: novas who have physically mutated past a certain point are now no longer fertile with anyone who doesn't have matching mutations (and since practically all novas are unique...). More humanlike novas can have all the babies they want. They're baseline babies, though. The only genetic oddness is that they're guaranteed to have the potential to erupt at some point.<br /> <br /> I think the sterilization conspiracy from 1e was super dumb. I strongly dislike the idea that a group PCs can belong to are the secret bad guys.<br /> <br /> (But what do I know, I also intended that bit in the Minerva section to be _history_, not a specific plot hook. That rogue agent is long gone. But he shows there can be rogue agents.What do you do if there's another one?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23899-topher-gerkey","name":"Topher Gerkey","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T07:32:07-08:00","id":1193107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Topher Gerkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1192927-nova-sterility-thoughts?p=1193070#post1193070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My personal preference: novas who have physically mutated past a certain point are now no longer fertile with anyone who doesn't have matching mutations (and since practically all novas are unique...). More humanlike novas can have all the babies they want. They're baseline babies, though. The only genetic oddness is that they're guaranteed to have the potential to erupt at some point.<br /> <br /> I think the sterilization conspiracy from 1e was super dumb. I strongly dislike the idea that a group PCs can belong to are the secret bad guys.<br /> <br /> (But what do I know, I also intended that bit in the Minerva section to be _history_, not a specific plot hook. That rogue agent is long gone. But he shows there can be rogue agents.What do you do if there's another one?)</div> </div> </div> </div>I support this as well. <br /> <br /> I especially like the idea that children of Novas are regular humans at birth but will erupt at some point. Maybe around puberty. I think this is 'better' than erupted as nova at birth. <br /> <br /> I too didn't like that Project Utopia was doimg so much bad. It makes it hard to like them at all. Which is frustrating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T08:40:04-08:00","id":1193143,"title":"","content":"Okay, I had a longer rant, but I compressed it.<br /> <br /> If Aeon sterilizes novas it's really only a matter of time before they find out. They will probably be smart enough to fix it. They will probably be very angry. People at Aeon is supposedly quite smart, so why OK this? How will that end well? It was stupid in 1st ed, but sure, suitably 90's grimdark conspiracy. Please lets avoid it this time, so we can maybe NOT feel like villains working for Aeon or Utopia.<br /> <br /> Though I agree that the sterilization as such isn't a bad setting mystery. But preferrably the underlying reason for it (this time) isn't crippling stupidity by people who supposedly believes in the best in humanity.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1226-gammelbraxen","name":"Gammelbraxen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T09:15:54-08:00","id":1193163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gammelbraxen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1192927-nova-sterility-thoughts?p=1193143#post1193143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, I had a longer rant, but I compressed it.<br /> <br /> If Aeon sterilizes novas it's really only a matter of time before they find out. They will probably be smart enough to fix it. They will probably be very angry. People at Aeon is supposedly quite smart, so why OK this? How will that end well? It was stupid in 1st ed, but sure, suitably 90's grimdark conspiracy. Please lets avoid it this time, so we can maybe NOT feel like villains working for Aeon or Utopia.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>^^ This. Yes. <br /> The whole problem in 1E was made worse by their implication of certain mega-intelligent novas (one of which was Antaeus) as not only aware of the plot but willing to allow it to continue unabated. There's no way that would happen, not when they could have thought of something better over morning coffee. Utopian mega-minds would have seen that plot coming a mile away and recognized that it was a bad idea, then isolated who was responsible (that paranoid twit Thetis and her ghoulish servitor Ozaki), and disposed of them in a hurry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T11:00:12-08:00","id":1193206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gammelbraxen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1192927-nova-sterility-thoughts?p=1193143#post1193143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, I had a longer rant, but I compressed it.<br /> <br /> If Aeon sterilizes novas it's really only a matter of time before they find out. They will probably be smart enough to fix it. They will probably be very angry. People at Aeon is supposedly quite smart, so why OK this? How will that end well? It was stupid in 1st ed, but sure, suitably 90's grimdark conspiracy. Please lets avoid it this time, so we can maybe NOT feel like villains working for Aeon or Utopia.<br /> <br /> Though I agree that the sterilization as such isn't a bad setting mystery. But preferrably the underlying reason for it (this time) isn't crippling stupidity by people who supposedly believes in the best in humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I agree on this. I think the Aeon sterilizes Novas is rather dumb. It also doesn't take into account how Nova age colonies don't have the issue. I think Second Generation should be rare and special even on places like Eden so the possiblity that its just &quot;a price of the Nova condition&quot; should be an option there or something on a Universal scale.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T11:57:15-08:00","id":1193238,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">While it is definitely possible that there could be a conspiracy to prevent Novas from procreating and possibly replacing humanity... I think there could be another possibility that may be a contributing factor. While the ability to manipulate Quantum (or even Psi) is genetic in nature, we do not know how dominant these genes are (they seem to be very recessive) and often seem to require an outside event to fully activate. The number of Novas even during the Nova Age was surprisingly small... in the hundreds world wide, and we have no idea how likely the genes that gave them their fantastic powers would be passed on to any children they might have... and even if they were, whether those children would manifest any powers at all.<br /> <br /> It is very possible that what might appear to be a conspiracy to sterilize all Novas to prevent them from having any children may merely be research to see how viable Novas (and Aberrants) are as a species. It is possible that their Nova nature naturally makes procreation (even with another Nova) difficult... the further the Nova (Aberrant) is from being human (with various mutations), the less likely that Nova would be able to procreate. Even those who are able to have children may not pass on the right genetics for the child to develop Nova powers... and even if they could, the conditions to bring out those powers may never happen. In short... the chances for two Novas being able to have a child together may be infinitesimally small... and the chance of that child developing Quantum Powers may be even smaller still... all without a dedicated conspiracy to prevent Novas from having children.<br /> <br /> Of course this doesn't mean there are not individuals who are so paranoid that even a 1 in a billion chance of Novas producing a Nova child is too great a risk... and will want to eliminate ANY chance of a 2nd Generation of Novas. Likewise it is also very possible that a sufficiently intelligent Nova could find a way to increase the chances of producing children (including those who can become Novas themselves)... something that would likely make those who fear Novas even more determined to prevent them from ever having children. All I am saying is that Quantum Power expression is one of the rarest forms of power in the Trinity Continuum... and it is hard to be sure if the low number is the result of simple nature or a deliberate conspiracy.<br /> <br /> It may just be that the Quantum Powers that make Nova's different... also makes procreation with others (baseline humans or other Novas) equally difficult. Just because all other aspects of Nova biology seem enhanced doesn't mean that they should be super fertile too. An active M-R node may naturally have the unintended side effect of reducing the viability of the Nova to produce children... or it may be that the Quantum Powers they use does the same thing... especially for those Novas that become noticeably inhuman in appearance.<br /> <br /> Both are viable options for why the Nova population remains surprisingly small... and are not mutually exclusive. In one timeline, it is possible that there is a conspiracy to render all Novas Sterile... while in another, it is merely their own unique genetics that does so... while in a third both contribute to keep Nova populations down... and a fourth timeline, neither is a factor and Novas become a new species of humanity (for good or ill). All things are possible within the Continuum.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T14:23:56-08:00","id":1193305,"title":"","content":"Honestly the more I thi k about it the more I LOVE the idea presented by Bunyip. The idea of it being a long term world wide low key Doyen supported psi based issue just really really really calls to me. <br /> <br /> The story potential is so grand. So the nova pcs follow the trail which leads them to an ancient department of the Aeon Society. They learn it started as a bit of research that someone took too far and then broke away from Aeon to create there own group. But then questions start to be raised which leads to answer indicating something caster, which leads to a base of operations on an island/mountain/city something like that. The operation through the base will eventually to the leader, someone infested by a Doyen, the dark heart of the conspiracy. The defeat of said Doyen leads to learning thar other conspiracies exist, including those which are even bigger dangers. <br /> <br /> In this alternate setup Project Utopia is working to find a cure, which shows their more positive nature. <br /> <br /> On the issue of nova children I think the answer is a matter of timing and the fact that children of Novas don't get access to there full power till around puberty. Till then they just have a healthy body and strong mind and maybe a simple bonus or two. <br /> <br /> But the thing is even those children of novas who were born right after the world wide eruption are no where near puberty and thus coming into there own. <br /> <br /> Just my thoughts. <br /> <br /> Oh, I also think the more Corrupted a nova is the less able to procreate with baselines they are. <br /> <br /> But yeah I never liked the whole &quot;nova children are born with powers fully active&quot; and much prefer &quot;children of Novas show improved body and mind but do not fully come into there powers until they reach puberty&quot;. <br /> <br /> This is necessary as an all quantum species needs to be allowed and automatic sterility is not really fitting for that. <br /> <br /> But yeah I REALLY like the idea of a Doyen conspiracy. Having such a thing ties Aberrant into the grester cosmology in a perfect way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T15:00:09-08:00","id":1193321,"title":"","content":"Wow, there's been a lot of vehement opposition. When I say &quot;an idea to consider&quot; I mean exactly that: I don't mean &quot;this is the new Aberrant canon.&quot; So please relax. That's not what I'm suggesting.<br /> <br /> I personally like the idea of that sort of tradeoff, where you get extra abilities and a lifespan potentially measured in centuries, but in exchange, you'll never have kids. That has a lot of interesting-to-me story potential. But &quot;would something like that work for Aberrant?&quot; is a very different question. Square pegs and round holes and all that.<br /> <br /> As you might surmise from the Trinity Continuum core, I like taking little sections and elements from stuff I love and smushing it together to make something new. That's my jam. Does it always work? No, but I have fun in the attempt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T16:52:12-08:00","id":1193358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1192927-nova-sterility-thoughts?p=1193321#post1193321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow, there's been a lot of vehement opposition. When I say &quot;an idea to consider&quot; I mean exactly that: I don't mean &quot;this is the new Aberrant canon.&quot; So please relax. That's not what I'm suggesting.<br /> <br /> I personally like the idea of that sort of tradeoff, where you get extra abilities and a lifespan potentially measured in centuries, but in exchange, you'll never have kids. That has a lot of interesting-to-me story potential. But &quot;would something like that work for Aberrant?&quot; is a very different question. Square pegs and round holes and all that.<br /> <br /> As you might surmise from the Trinity Continuum core, I like taking little sections and elements from stuff I love and smushing it together to make something new. That's my jam. Does it always work? No, but I have fun in the attempt.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I know there always a risk of compromising narratives and getting neither goal when one tries to take a middle-path, but I think this is a &quot;have your cake and eat it too&quot; circumstance. Whether it's a natural byproduct of eruption, or part of a vast complex conspiracy like Bunyip described, it's possible to include the narrative consequences of widespread infertility with exceptions that allow for the &quot;second generation&quot; narrative - if anything the rarity of the second gen would heighten the cases of said narrative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T17:24:09-08:00","id":1193366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1192927-nova-sterility-thoughts?p=1193321#post1193321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow, there's been a lot of vehement opposition. When I say &quot;an idea to consider&quot; I mean exactly that: I don't mean &quot;this is the new Aberrant canon.&quot; So please relax. That's not what I'm suggesting.<br /> <br /> I personally like the idea of that sort of tradeoff, where you get extra abilities and a lifespan potentially measured in centuries, but in exchange, you'll never have kids. That has a lot of interesting-to-me story potential. But &quot;would something like that work for Aberrant?&quot; is a very different question. Square pegs and round holes and all that.<br /> <br /> As you might surmise from the Trinity Continuum core, I like taking little sections and elements from stuff I love and smushing it together to make something new. That's my jam. Does it always work? No, but I have fun in the attempt.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I am more open to the idea that all things are possible rather than a definitive &quot;this is the one and only truth&quot; that tries to force players into one style of play. Perhaps the low birth rate is inherent to Novas... perhaps there is a conspiracy to make it that way... perhaps it is both... perhaps it is neither. Allowing individual groups to decide what the truth is for their own games allows for every possible outcome... even when the group decides on one specific outcome for their game.<br /> <br /> If I want to run a game where Project Utopia is actually innocent of any plot to sterilize the Novas (either because they never did so or because it was a rogue element trying to do so), I want that to be just as plausible as if I were to take part in a game where Project Utopia was deliberately trying to do so. While many may think that only one can be &quot;official&quot;, the truth is that both can be if written well (such as leaving it for individual groups to decide what is true for their game)... and leaving the truth for the Continuum as a whole vague and mysterious.<br /> <br /> When all options are possible... everyone can be right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T00:06:22-08:00","id":1193457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowstripe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1192927-nova-sterility-thoughts?p=1193366#post1193366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If I want to run a game where Project Utopia is actually innocent of any plot to sterilize the Novas (either because they never did so or because it was a rogue element trying to do so), I want that to be just as plausible as if I were to take part in a game where Project Utopia was deliberately trying to do so.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it might be refreshing for Utopia to actually BE good instead of merely trying to <i>appear</i> good. Maybe it was just part of my mindset in the 90s but I assumed any organization trying to be that good was automatically evil at the core. A rogue agent could steal information about biochemicals that are deleterious to a naturally lessened nova fertility and then run off to some other place to try and spread it everywhere, all without them being an implausibly obvious festering tumor inside of Utopia itself. In our current world Utopia is likely to be stymied enough by the corporate oligarchy actively (and subtly) opposing almost every economic goodwill plan they try, or being assailed by the bought-out media whenever they make ANY mistake, it seems like kicking the dog to have this kind of thing hanging over them too unless they're being framed.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T00:44:39-08:00","id":1193462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1192927-nova-sterility-thoughts?p=1193457#post1193457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it might be refreshing for Utopia to actually BE good instead of merely trying to <i>appear</i> good.</div> </div> </div> </div>To a certain value of &quot;good&quot;, I agree. For &quot;Aberrant&quot; to be a valid heroic Alignment, Project Utopia can't be objectively in the right. But that can be accomplished through valid philosophical differences rather than nefarious conspiracy.<br /> <br /> There also should be room for clandestine conspiracies in any faction, but that can be done without it being as defining and in control of the faction as with what happened with Project Utopia in 1st edition. So corruption can exist and Aberrant be in part a response to said corruption, without said corruption making Project Utopia heroes complicit and inherently in the wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 03-09-2018, 03:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T05:16:21-08:00","id":1193491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1192927-nova-sterility-thoughts?p=1193009#post1193009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Make it difficult to cure. Various novas should have been able to easily shake off the sterilization, but make it more of a challenging quest in 2e. The way to do this is relatively simple - make the affliction psi based*. The conspiracy doesn\u2019t know why this special compound is so anti nova (and harmless to normal humans), but they know that it is. This gives story hooks and a trail of evidence that goes way back, to some group who studied stalwarts and Mesmerists, and noticed a tiny but statistically significant adversarial aspect to how their powers worked. Maybe this original group had no negative implications - maybe they just studied. But somewhere along the way, when novas appeared, someone else got hold of their research and synthesised the chemical and worked out how to make it global.<br /> <br /> (Maybe some lost, solitary Doyen was stranded on Earth, couldn\u2019t escape out of the barrier, and used its psi powers to modify Eath chemistry and organisms to produce this chemical as a terrified form of self Defence.)<br /> <br /> A conspiracy is fine, IMO, but it needs to be something to be defeated. In the 1e games I ran, this was certainly the case, but it was too easy to discover and defeat.<br /> <br /> * But such tiny amounts of psi that it does nothing to hinder the novas powers, but is incredibly hard for anything quantum-based to remove.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having the Doyen be an active part of the sterilization conspiracy is certainly one route to go.<br /> <br /> Another would be for a Nova with something like Ecological Supremacy (able to make entire species more or less fertile, as just one thing they can do). An unknown Nova (perhaps one that predates the Galatea explosion) may have decided to slow things down by making all of these new Novas infertile. Or it could be a known Nova, such as Spencer 'Antaeus' Balmer (IIRC, too lazy to look his name up...). The reasons could be because the individual wants to minimize the disruption to the human world that the sudden appearance of Novas is causing (by preventing them from exploding in population through reproduction, as well as eruption), or they have foreseen somehow that 2nd and later generation Novas will be more powerful, or less human, or significantly more disruptive somehow, or it could be as selfish as the instigator wants to keep the number of Novas low, under the theory that the more of them there are, the less special and unique the Novas who already exist are, or that the more Novas erupt, the more could erupt (or be born) with power levels that could challenge the 'first Novas' (such as Mal). Jeremiah Scripture would be a freaky choice to be involved in such a conspiracy, seeking to prevent a 2nd generation from eventually arising to surpass the power of Divis Mal.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23754-ian-turner","name":"Ian Turner","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T07:07:27-08:00","id":1193535,"title":"","content":"I definitely like the idea of the Doyen being one possible option, especially because the idea of being able to reveal and confront the Doyen in the early 21st century seems like an interesting way for the continuum to branch in a given game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23646-goblinsociety","name":"GoblinSociety","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T08:14:34-08:00","id":1193559,"title":"","content":"To be honest, I am really hoping that they won't focus so much on this one aspect of the game... yes, the possibility of forced sterility upon Novas can be an interesting plot to uncover... if you are into such things... but to be honest, I think Novas should generally have bigger things to worry about.<br /> <br /> There are many other plots that could lead to similar conflicts between Novas and those trying to control them. Sure... there could be an actual conspiracy to sterilize them so they can't produce more... or it may just be a baseless theory (well, maybe not entirely baseless if this is natural for Novas) that some are using to try and distract people from something else. What could that something else be? Almost anything... there were many things going on in the original Aberrant game than just figuring out why Novas couldn't procreate.<br /> <br /> Let the low birthrate be something mysterious for players to play with as they see fit (don't give a definitive answer as to why it is... let groups decide the answer for their game) and move on to more interesting problems to be dealt with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T08:40:09-08:00","id":1193570,"title":"","content":"I was just thinking on how we nitpick the things we don't like but often don't say anything about that which we do enjoy. <br /> <br /> So I don't like the sterility and how it's done by Project Utopia, I want my pc faction to be a trusted good group, but I like hundreds of pages of story, setting, timeline, and powers of the book. <br /> <br /> So I think having it be mentioned as a potential worry in the front part of the book is great but then have it be explained farther in the secrets chapter where potential Doyen involvement is mentioned. <br /> <br /> But yeah what bothered me the most was how it waa Utopia doing it. That ruined Project Utopia for me almost entirely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T04:39:11-07:00","id":1196766,"title":"","content":"I'm still confused on Nova fertility. Is it assumed they that they have a hard time reproducing successfully or is it more most of them are sterile and an exceptional few aren't?<br /> <br /> And what about a compromise issue, with Nova's having normal fertility but producing Inspired level (Stalwarts) offspring who occasionally fully erupt into Novas.<br /> <br /> Do we have any talk about Nova Children? Are they always normal and erupting into power later in life, or are some born with super strength or mind powers?<br /> <br /> And is there talk about their powers being inherited, and therefore similar, or is it more each Nova is a blank slate and can erupt into any power?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T09:07:45-07:00","id":1196818,"title":"","content":"<i>Aberrant </i>isn't written yet, so it's all speculation. Don't take anything from the first edition as gospel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23899-topher-gerkey","name":"Topher Gerkey","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T09:53:29-07:00","id":1197244,"title":"","content":"Back in 1st ed they never really came out and said novas had less or more fertility in their natural state. Everyone just assumed they were sterile thanks to Proteus propaganda and their biochemical sterility agent. Nova couples who had kids pre-eruption still had those baseline kids, but there was never any mention of what else happened in this case, it was just a side-detail that got glossed over.<br /> Also back in 1st ed the subject of nova children being more powerful than 1st gen novas came up when you peruse the Proteus info in the Utopia book. It's prolly one of the main reasons they were trying to kill that off ASAP. <br /> <br /> It's looking like for Aberrant 2.0 people might prefer that nova fertility be somewhat staggered for any number of reasons but not destroyed. Perhaps a given fertile couple of novas under typical conditions has a single nova child in their entire long lifespan, since they have way lees to worry about from a survival standpoint they naturally don't need to breed very fast like some of the people who have 4-7 child households.<br /> It may be just me, but for the issue of 2nd generation novas it could be better to make them more &quot;stable&quot; and less likely to accrue taint by virtue of being born with quantum power, rather than more powerful. If a 1st gen can already reach level 6 quantum powers given time that pretty much caps out the power scale.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}